        <ArticleTitle>Hypertension &amp; cardiovascular risk &#x2013; a <i>cohort</i> study of <sup>24</sup>-hour ambulatory blood pressure</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Elevated blood pressure is a leading modifiable risk factor for cardiovascular disease worldwide.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">Over a median follow-up of 8.2 years, each 10-mmHg increase in systolic blood pressure was associated with a hazard ratio of 1.42 (95% CI 1.31-1.54).</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
